# <type>[optional scope]: <description>
# 
# [optional body]
# 
# ---
# Allowed Types:
#   feat     : A new feature (e.g., feat(auth): add login endpoint)
#   fix      : A bug fix (e.g., fix(user): resolve foreign key violation)
#   refactor : A code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   chore    : Routine tasks, maintenance, dependency updates
#   docs     : Documentation changes
#   test     : Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests
#   style    : Changes that do not affect the meaning of the code
#   perf     : A code change that improves performance
# 
# Rules:
# 1. Lowercase Type (e.g., feat)
# 2. Imperative Mood (e.g., "add feature", not "added feature")
# 3. No Period at the end of the subject line
# 4. Use the body to explain what and why (vs. how)
